00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:12.110
the insole start to flatten out just from
the weight of the person wearing them.

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:14.700
Uh, and I was starting to have knee pain again.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:20.260
So I wanted to go to a podiatrist, get a new
evaluation, find out if I need new insoles,

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.320
uh, and also have them look at my feet.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:27.540
I have something called Greek feet hilariously,
where the second toe is longer than the big

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:32.600
toe and it can sometimes scrunch that second
toe and uh, create some weird stuff on the

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:33.820
front of the foot and the nail.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.220
So I wanted that looked at as well.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.220
Okay.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:37.420
So I made an appointment with my podiatrist.

