00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:10.940
Now how could this be?

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.069
I paid my $40 copay.

00:03:13.069 --> 00:03:15.590
I didn't need authorization, I didn't need
a referral.

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:16.790
Podiatry is covered.

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:18.810
I went to a podiatrist covered by my plan.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:25.120
Well, it turns out, uh, that podiatry is covered
and I didn't need a referral and I didn't

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.660
need preauthorization.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:33.010
But the diagnosis of flat feet is not covered.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:35.540
And that is how I was diagnosed.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:43.210
And therefore io $454 for the visit minus
the $40 copay or $414.

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:45.200
So I say, wait, hold on a second.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.930
I went in for knee pain.

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:52.000
How should I know in advance what the diagnosis
is going to be?

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.640
My insurance says that simply not our problem.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:59.750
So anyway, I was able to speak to someone
who said what you should do is call the doctor

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:03.640
and ask if this is definitely wink, wink,
the right diagnosis.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:08.990
Now of course someone at Tufts health plan
can't say, David, let me help you commit insurance.

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:12.849
Call the doctor and ask for a different diagnosis
so that we will cover them.

00:04:12.849 --> 00:04:16.160
Obviously they can't do that, but I'm reading
between the lines and they say, this is the

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:17.160
system we have.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:20.419
I would call the doctor's office and explain
the situation.

00:04:20.419 --> 00:04:24.110
So I called the doctor's office and I explained
and they say, oh, we're going to get someone

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:25.840
to talk to the doctor.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:32.430
Maybe the doctor can rebuild this some other
way, maybe focusing on the Greek feet part

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:35.160
or some other diagnosis other than flat feet.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:40.130
So at this point, again, fortunately this
is more a curiosity for me.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.710
Can I ultimately get this covered?

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:49.150
I may well end up paying three 75 for the
insults, four 14 for the visit, plus my $40

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:50.150
Copay, right?

00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:57.990
That's $829 in addition to my monthly insurance
premium of $425 a month to get insults.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.259
Okay?

00:04:59.259 --> 00:05:05.050
In other countries in souls are 100 bucks
and the podiatrist themselves makes them and

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:07.159
it would be a fraction of the cost.

00:05:07.159 --> 00:05:11.770
So understand that part of the inefficiency
